{"entryId":"2903","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2903:1","sourceSha256":"614ba1ee7d167848aed82055981841816d7d6b8821f93803195763dfe92ca743","englishSha256":"42227533da9878feaa5e670929ce78c7f42caf7c33efc9f861a4a26d952025c8","citations":[{"id":"2903:1:link-01","he":[45,59],"en":[131,141],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_52b.5"},"reference":"Gittin 52b:5","assessment":"The passage identifies Amram as the dyer and guardian of orphans.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 52b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_52b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 52b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_52b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The passage identifies Amram as the dyer and guardian of orphans.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Gittin spells Rav Naḥman fully and explicitly has the orphans’ relatives appear. The pinned Hebrew has a singular verb.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The narrative assigns a guardianship role. Retain Heilprin’s explicit uncertainty about whether the dyer was a sage.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 52b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_52b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 52b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_52b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
